  "caption": "Quinn's app planned training by cycle phase, so squats kept getting skipped.\n\nKay explains that the link between cycle phase and injury risk is weak. Consistent training and eating enough for your training tend to matter more, and there's no need to avoid heavy sessions in set phases. Missed periods in athletes are a warning sign.\n\nWhat can help: train consistently rather than by app phase, track symptoms and adjust a single week if you notice a clear pattern, eat enough to support bone health, and practise landing and change-of-direction technique.\n\nTalk to your GP or physio if periods stop while training hard, bleeding is heavy, there's bone pain with weight bearing, or a knee gives way.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
